HOW TO ATTRIBUTE

  Minimum credit, wherever the data or a database derived from it is published:

      Price and model data from Prumo (https://github.com/Navesz/prumo),
      licensed CC BY 4.0. Modified: yes / no.

  Two further requests, which are how this dataset stays honest rather than
  extra legal conditions:

  1. Keep the per-row stamp. Every price row carries fonte (the URL it was read
     from), coletado_em (the date it was read) and metodo (doc, medido, or
     estimado). A price stripped of its date is folklore again — that stamp is
     the entire difference between this catalogue and a README table, and it is
     why rows older than 30 days drop out of Prumo's ranking on their own.

  2. Mark your edits at the row level, not only in a footer. An unmarked change
     makes the original source appear to assert a price it never asserted, and
     the provider is the one who gets blamed for it.

  Attribution must not suggest that Prumo, its contributors, or any provider
  endorses you or your use.

