  Accuracy is not warranted, and this matters more here than in most datasets:
  as of 2026-08-24 every row is documentation reading, not measurement, and
  nothing has been confirmed against a real invoice. Before any number here is
  used to spend money, check it against the provider.

CORRECTION AND REMOVAL

  A provider who wants a row corrected or removed does not need to argue about
  copyright first. Open an issue at https://github.com/Navesz/prumo/issues using
  the price-correction template, identifying the rows. For a request that should
  not be public, use the private reporting form at
  https://github.com/Navesz/prumo/security/advisories/new and begin the summary
  with [Catalogue]; a draft advisory is readable only by you and the maintainer.

  Rows are corrected or pulled from the published catalogue first and discussed
  after — a wrong price in a tool that routes money is worse for the provider
  than a missing one.
